1
00:00:00,180 --> 00:00:03,240
This man survived sixty hours inside a sunken ship.

2
00:00:03,560 --> 00:00:05,400
Nigeria, May 2013.

3
00:00:05,420 --> 00:00:07,500
The tug Jascon-4 capsized.

4
00:00:07,700 --> 00:00:10,030
The cook, Harrison Okene, was in the toilet.

5
00:00:10,280 --> 00:00:13,050
It settled on the seabed, about thirty metres down.

6
00:00:13,320 --> 00:00:15,230
In the dark, he found a pocket of air.

7
00:00:15,410 --> 00:00:16,810
About four feet high.

8
00:00:17,160 --> 00:00:19,070
Every breath made that air more toxic.

9
00:00:19,330 --> 00:00:21,260
Eleven crewmates never made it out.

10
00:00:21,750 --> 00:00:23,500
On day three, divers arrived.

11
00:00:23,620 --> 00:00:24,890
Not to rescue anyone.

12
00:00:24,910 --> 00:00:26,050
To recover bodies.

13
00:00:26,440 --> 00:00:28,270
On the camera feed, a hand appeared.

14
00:00:28,460 --> 00:00:30,580
Everyone assumed it was another body.

15
00:00:31,160 --> 00:00:32,700
Then the hand grabbed him.

16
00:00:33,070 --> 00:00:33,910
Okene was alive.

17
00:00:33,930 --> 00:00:35,430
But he couldn't just swim up.

18
00:00:35,690 --> 00:00:38,240
Days at depth had saturated his body with gas.

19
00:00:38,430 --> 00:00:40,220
A fast ascent could have killed him.

20
00:00:40,480 --> 00:00:42,680
They brought him up into a decompression chamber.

21
00:00:42,980 --> 00:00:46,970
One expert estimated the air turned dangerous around hour fifty-six.

22
00:00:47,150 --> 00:00:48,790
He was found near hour sixty.

23
00:00:49,180 --> 00:00:51,330
They came for the dead and found him breathing.
